Font atlas v3 → v4: a kerning-pair section appended after coverage. The baker
walks GPOS lookupType 2 (format 1 pair sets and format 2 class defs, class 0
reconstructed from coverage) and writes i8 logical-px deltas. The core applies
them in measure_run and layout_run. A core that cannot apply the pairs refuses
the blob; v2 and v3 still load.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

2026-10-22, rebased onto 66caf4e5. Main gained atlas readers and writers
that assumed v3: `framework/src/font-coverage.ts` (the baked-coverage check)
reads v4, whose header and cmap are v3's; `hosts/web/runtime-glyphs.js`
parses v4 and carries the kern section through an append;
`tools/companion/glyphs.ts` writes v3 by name, its cells having no pairs.
Main's fallback faces put a glyph in a slot whose id is the FALLBACK face's;
such a glyph is keyed -1 so the slot face's GPOS pairs cannot match it.
Measured before the fix: Inter at 24 px with Noto Sans CJK behind it put a
-1 px pair between '7' and '二'. Five of main's core tests that filled
"coverage to the end of the blob" now stop before the v4 kern section.

